---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About ImageLab & Open-Source Credits | ImageLab"
  description="Learn how ImageLab delivers fast, private image conversion, compression, PDF tools, and AI OCR right inside your browser."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pb-14 space-y-8 animate-fade-up">
    <header>
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-400 mb-2">About</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950">
        Built for Speed &amp; Verifiable Privacy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 mt-2.5 leading-relaxed">
        ImageLab is a browser-first image and PDF studio built so anyone can convert, compress,
        crop, redact, watermark, extract text, and manage PDFs quickly without signups, daily
        paywalls, or intrusive clutter.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="studio-card rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">Why Browser-First Architecture?</h2>
        <p>
          Traditional online converters upload your personal portraits, signatures, invoices, and
          PDFs to remote servers and cap free users to a few tasks per day. By running
          high-efficiency WebAssembly image codecs and local PDF engines inside background Web
          Workers, ImageLab keeps core tools instant, unlimited, and strictly private on your device.
          For tasks that need modern multimodal vision—such as bilingual English &amp; Bengali OCR—we
          use encrypted, zero-storage serverless processing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">Verify Zero Uploads Yourself</h2>
        <p>
          Open your browser’s <strong>DevTools → Network</strong> tab (press <code>F12</code>),
          clear the log, and run any image conversion, compression, crop, blur, EXIF cleanup, or
          PDF tool on ImageLab. You will see zero file upload requests leaving your device.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">Testing &amp; Editorial Standards</h2>
        <p>
          Every tool and technical guide published in our{' '}
          <a href="/guides" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline">Guides hub</a> is
          tested across desktop and mobile browsers against real camera captures (JPG, PNG, WEBP,
          AVIF, and iOS HEIC) and multi-page PDF documents. We enforce magic-byte validation,
          memory-safe canvas caps, and permissive open-source licensing across the stack.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">Open-Source Credits &amp; Licenses</h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500">
          ImageLab is powered by trusted permissive open-source libraries (MIT, Apache-2.0, and BSD).
          Our frontend repository is public on{' '}
          <a
            href="https://github.com/thethirdclasseditor-ship-it/imagelab-free"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>
          .
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-zinc-600 list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>Astro, React, Tailwind CSS &amp; Lucide Icons</strong> — MIT / ISC licenses</li>
          <li><strong>@jsquash/jpeg (MozJPEG) &amp; @jsquash/webp (LibWebP)</strong> — Apache-2.0 / BSD licenses</li>
          <li><strong>UPNG.js, JSZip, jsPDF, pdf-lib, exifr &amp; heic-to</strong> — MIT licenses</li>
          <li><strong>PDF.js (pdfjs-dist)</strong> — Apache-2.0 license</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
